Neither the bootloader nor the UKIs will remain unchanged over time. Updates to
systemd-boot or the kernel will result in either UKIs or the bootloader binary
being overwritten. Every time this happens, these files need to be resigned. To
ensure this happens automatically, we will create a hook for pacman that will
sign the bootloader binaries every time they are updated. For the kernel, we
will edit uki.conf to make signing the UKI files part of their build process.

After these steps have completed succesfully, we will simulate an update to the
bootloader to trigger the signing process. We could simply sign all the files
directly but this way ensures that our setup was complete and will continue to
work in the future.
